h Claypole","aliases":["Noah","Mr. Claypole"],"role":"supporting","firstAppearance":"s5","summary":"First mention: “Take down the shutters, yer idle young ruffian!” With this, Mr.”"},{"id":"charley-bates","name":"Charley Bates","aliases":["Master Bates","Charley"],"role":"supporting","firstAppearance":"s9","summary":"First mention: “He had scarcely washed himself, and made everything tidy, by emptying the basin out of the window, agreeably to the Jew’s directions, when the Dodger returned: accompanied by a very sprightly young friend, whom Oliver…”"},{"id":"monks","name":"Monks","role":"supporting","firstAppearance":"s26","summary":"First mention: ““Monks, do you mean?”"},{"id":"mr-giles","name":"Mr. Giles","aliases":["Giles"],"role":"supporting","firstAppearance":"s28","summary":"First mention: ““I am agreeable to anything which is agreeable to Mr.”"},{"id":"artful-dodger","name":"Artful Dodger","aliases":["Dodger"],"role":"supporting","firstAppearance":"s8","summary":"First mention: “Dawkins’s appearance did not say a vast deal in favour of the comforts which his patron’s interest obtained for those whom he took under his protection; but, as he had a rather flightly and dissolute mode of conversin…”"},{"id":"nancy","name":"Nancy","role":"supporting","firstAppearance":"s9","summary":"First mention: “When this game had been played a great many times, a couple of young ladies called to see the young gentleman; one of whom was named Bet, and the other Nancy.”"},{"id":"bill","name":"Bill","role":"supporting","firstAppearance":"s5","summary":"First mention: ““Now, Bill!”"},{"id":"toby-crackit","name":"Toby Crackit","aliases":["Toby","Crackit","Mr. Crackit"],"role":"supporting","firstAppearance":"s19","summary":"First mention: “I tell you that Toby Crackit has been hanging about the place for a fortnight, and he can’t get one of the servants in line.””"},{"id":"mrs-corney","name":"Mrs. Corney","role":"supporting","firstAppearance":"s23","summary":"First mention: “Such was the aspect of out-of-doors affairs, when Mrs.”"},{"id":"mrs-mann","name":"Mrs. Mann","role":"supporting","firstAppearance":"s2","summary":"First mention: “Be this as it may, however, it _was_ his ninth birthday; and he was keeping it in the coal-cellar with a select party of two other young gentleman, who, after participating with him in a sound thrashing, had been lock…”"},{"id":"mr-grimwig","name":"Mr. Grimwig","role":"supporting","firstAppearance":"s14","summary":"First mention: “Bumble, a peculiarly impatient little double-knock was heard at the street-door: and the servant, running upstairs, announced Mr.”"},{"id":"mrs-maylie","name":"Mrs. Maylie","role":"minor","group":"g-maylie","firstAppearance":"s29","summary":"First mention: ““My dear Mrs.”"},{"id":"harry-maylie","name":"Harry Maylie","aliases":["Harry"],"role":"minor","group":"g-maylie","firstAppearance":"s33","summary":"First mention: “Oliver glanced at it, and saw that it was directed to Harry Maylie, Esquire, at some great lord’s house in the country; where, he could not make out.”"},{"id":"charlotte","name":"Charlotte","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s4","summary":"First mention: ““Here, Charlotte,” said Mr.”"},{"id":"tom-chitling","name":"Tom Chitling","aliases":["Mr. Chitling","Tom","Chitling"],"role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s18","summary":"First mention: “The conversation proceeded no farther at this time, for the Jew had returned home accompanied by Miss Betsy, and a gentleman whom Oliver had never seen before, but who was accosted by the Dodger as Tom Chitling; and w…”"},{"id":"brittles","name":"Brittles","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s28","summary":"First mention: ““You are afraid, Brittles,” said Mr.”"},{"id":"mr-losberne","name":"Mr. Losberne","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s29","summary":"First mention: “Giles upstairs; and while he is going upstairs, the reader may be informed, that Mr.”"},{"id":"mr-bolter","name":"Mr. Bolter","aliases":["Bolter"],"role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s42","summary":"First mention: ““Mr.”"},{"id":"blathers","name":"Blathers","aliases":["Mr. Blathers"],"role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s31","summary":"First mention: ““Tell your governor that Blathers and Duff is here, will you?”"},{"id":"mrs-sowerberry","name":"Mrs. Sowerberry","role":"minor","group":"g-sowerberry","firstAppearance":"s4","summary":"First mention: ““Mrs.”"},{"id":"mr-fang","name":"Mr. Fang","aliases":["Fang"],"role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s11","summary":"First mention: “He closed his book hastily; and was at once ushered into the imposing presence of the renowned Mr.”"},{"id":"barney","name":"Barney","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s15","summary":"First mention: ““Is anybody here, Barney?”"},{"id":"mr-sowerberry","name":"Mr. Sowerberry","role":"minor","group":"g-sowerberry","firstAppearance":"s4","summary":"First mention: “Bumble had been despatched to make various preliminary inquiries, with the view of finding out some captain or other who wanted a cabin-boy without any friends; and was returning to the workhouse to communicate the re…”"},{"id":"mr-gamfield","name":"Mr. Gamfield","aliases":["Gamfield"],"role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s3","summary":"First mention: “It chanced one morning, while Oliver’s affairs were in this auspicious and comfortable state, that Mr.”"},{"id":"mrs-bedwin","name":"Mrs. Bedwin","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s12","summary":"First mention: “He is not hungry, Mrs.”"},{"id":"mrs-bumble","name":"Mrs. Bumble","role":"minor","group":"g-bumble","firstAppearance":"s37","summary":"First mention: ““Mrs.”"}],"relationships":[{"id":"r1","source":"mrs-mann","target":"oliver-twist","weight":16,"phases":[{"at":"s2","type":"together","label":"Often together","weight":14}]},{"id":"r2","source":"mr-bumble","target":"oliver-twist","weight":99,"phases":[{"at":"s2","type":"together","label":"Often together","weight":15},{"at":"s4","type":"together","label":"Constantly together","weight":49}]},{"id":"r3","source":"mr-bumble